**CBS \- LG \- Legal/General Counsel’s Office (GCO) :**
 Our enablement functions help everyone at EY operate more efficiently. As a CBS professional, you will work across teams to provide the knowledge, resources and tools that help EY deliver exceptional quality service to our clients, win in the marketplace and support EY’s growth and profitability. Major teams within CBS include Finance, Information Technology, Human Resources, Enterprise Support Services, Admin, Brand, Marketing and Communications, Quality and Risk Management.




 With so many offerings, you have the opportunity to develop your career through a broad scope of engagements, mentoring and formal learning. We aim to develop outstanding leaders who team to deliver on our promises to all of our stakeholders, besides playing a critical role in building a better working world for our people, clients and communities.




**Your Key Responsibilities**
**Technical Excellence**
* Job Description for Executive\-Litigation;
* To coordinate with external lawyers and internal stakeholders for drafting, managing, distribution, providing responses to, for all litigation and regulatory queries/requirements;
* To interact and work closely with multiple stakeholders (including internal and external) in relation to all legal matters;
* Tackle complex issues that cross organisational and geographical boundaries and advice on any issue that the business functions face;
* Wealth of experience in advising on compliance and legal issues;
* Develop clear understanding of EY policies and procedures;
* Proficiency with the applicable laws (with emphasis on corporate laws and data privacy laws), legal procedures, protocols and functioning of various courts and tribunals in India;
* Basic understanding of GDPR and reviewing data processing agreements;
* Drafting, vetting, reviewing, contractual agreements, RFPs, NDAs, with knowledge of internal stakeholder's expectations and ability to fulfil its requirements;
* Drafting and filing legal documents and/or correspondences to be sent from the General Counsel’s Office;
* Transcribing minutes of meetings, case preparation, notes for case files, briefs for the General Counsel and/or other stakeholders;
* Coordination with the team members for preparation of presentations/decks/guidance documents;
* Efficient case tracking and management skills for all matters with timely and regular briefs being sent to the General Counsel for all matters;
* Review of contract terms and conditions to verify that they are in compliance with firm’s policies and all applicable laws and identify any potential/threats of litigation;
* Adept at legal research, legal analysis and certain litigation support activities (as may be required);
* 8\+ years of experience in law firms or in\-house legal team of multi\-national companies;
* Ability to manage multiple priorities, work efficiently under pressure and consistently meet tight deadlines;
* Client/internal stakeholder management skills;
* Comfortable with working on pace and functioning in a hands on environment;
* Fluent in verbal and written English; and
* Short notice period. To coordinate with external lawyers and internal stakeholders for drafting, managing, for all litigation and regulatory queries/requirements; Basic understanding of GDPR case preparation, notes for case files, briefs for the General Counsel and/or other stakeholders.


**Skills And Attributes**
**To qualify for the role you must have**
**Qualification**
* LLB


**Experience**
* 8\+ Years in law/legal field


**What We Look For**
 People with the ability to work in a collaborative manner to provide services across multiple client departments while following the commercial and legal requirements. You will need a practical approach to solving issues and complex problems with the ability to deliver insightful and practical solutions. We look for people who are agile, curious, mindful, and able to sustain positive energy, while being adaptable and creative in their approach.




**What We Offer**
 Fuelled by the brilliance of our people, EY has emerged as the strongest brand and the most attractive employer in our field, with market\-leading growth over competitors. Our people work side\-by\-side with market\-leading entrepreneurs, game\-changers, disruptors, and visionaries. As an organization, we are investing more time, technology, and money than ever before in skills and learning for our people. At EY, you will have a personalized Career Journey and also the chance to tap into the resources of our career frameworks to better know about your roles, skills, and opportunities.




 EY is equally committed to being an inclusive employer, and we strive to achieve the right balance for our people—enabling us to deliver excellent client service while allowing our people to build their careers as well as focus on their wellbeing.




 If you can confidently demonstrate that you meet the criteria above, please contact us as soon as possible.




 Join us in shaping the future with confidence. Apply Now
